    "created_at": "2016-05-04T13:13:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-04T13:13:25Z",
    "body": "The spec as currently written says: \n\n> rel's supported tokens are the keywords defined in HTML link types which are allowed on link elements, impact the processing model, and are supported by the user agent. The possible supported tokens are alternate, icon, pingback, prefetch, stylesheet and next.\n> ....\n> Other specifications may add HTML link types as defined in Other link types, with the following additional requirements:\n\nI hadn't realized that \"search\" is defined by HTML but isn't in the \"possible supported tokens\" list.  I guess I can take it out of the Firefox `supports()` implementation if that's preferable, but this one does seem like something sites might want to detect and offer alternate UI for if it's not supported.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
