    "created_at": "2016-05-16T11:32:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-16T11:32:15Z",
    "body": "I kinda like maintaining a subset in \"possible supported tokens\", and only add keywords to it where it makes sense to feature-test for it, because that makes it more likely we end up in an interoperable state of Web-exposed behavior. If some browser has some special UI for some keywords but Web developers are not trying to check for it and provide a fallback, then there's no reason to include it in \"possible supported tokens\" in my opinion.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
